Upstream Benchmark License & Attribution Notice
===============================================

1. Imported SAT Competition 2023 & 2024 CNF Instances (`*.cnf`) and
   Derived Equivalent AIGER Conversions (`aig-version/*.aig`):

   These 14 benchmark formulas were sourced from the International SAT
   Competition 2023 and 2024 Main Tracks:
     - SAT Competition 2023: https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/
     - SAT Competition 2024: https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/
     - Global Benchmark Database (GBD): https://benchmark-database.de/
     - GBD tooling (MIT License): https://github.com/Udopia/gbd

   International SAT Competition benchmark archives (published via the SAT
   Competition proceedings and Zenodo archives) are distributed under the
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0):
     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Under CC-BY-4.0 you are free to share and adapt the benchmark files for any
   purpose, provided appropriate attribution is given to the original benchmark
   authors and the International SAT Competition / Global Benchmark Database.
   Exact 32-character GBD MD5 identifiers and provenance metadata for every
   instance are preserved in `src/sc23_24_manifest.json`.

